Description:
When importing a work through the API on behalf of an author that doesn't have an email address, the import fails with the following message:

{code}
Error 'undefined method `each' for nil:NilClass"
{code}

This is due to the StoryParser returning {{nil}} when it processes an author with no email address. The problem isn't visible when doing an archivist import through the Work Import form because the email address field is required in the front-end. 

ETA: Given AO3-5058 which was logged recently, the statement about the email being required on the front-end may have been incorrect and is certainly not true now.

When performing imports through the API, the Open Doors team are getting this error increasingly frequently:

{code}
Mysql2::Error: Duplicate entry '18401233-Chapter-796508' for key 'creation_id_creation_type_pseud_id': INSERT INTO `creatorships` (`created_at`, `creation_id`, `creation_type`, `pseud_id`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('2016-09-14 11:56:33', 18401233, 'Chapter', 796508, '2016-09-14 11:56:33')
{code}

As far as we can tell, this did not happen at all prior to September 2016. It happened a couple of times to stories in the last two imports, but is now happening all the time for the current import and has suddenly become a major blocker.

