Description:
We'd like to be able to rate limit searches (including filtering). Luckily, we have Rack::Attack\! So let's put that to work.

There will be two rate limit settings. One will be for bookmarks ({{unicorn_elastic_bookmarks}}), the other ({{unicorn_elastic}}) will be for everything else. 

{noformat}URL                                 LIMIT SET BY
"~/collections/.*/works"            "unicorn_elastic" ;
"~/collections/.*/tags/.*/works"    "unicorn_elastic" ;
"~/collections/.*/bookmarks"        "unicorn_elastic_bookmarks" ;
"~/tags/search.*"                   "unicorn_elastic" ;
"~/people/search.*"                 "unicorn_elastic" ;
"~/works/search.*"                  "unicorn_elastic" ;
"~/tags/.*/works"                   "unicorn_elastic" ;
"~/tags/.*/bookmarks"               "unicorn_elastic_bookmarks" ;
"~/users/.*/works"                  "unicorn_elastic" ;
"~/users/.*/bookmarks"              "unicorn_elastic_bookmarks" ;
"~/works/collected"                 "unicorn_elastic" ;
"~/bookmarks/search.*"              "unicorn_elastic_bookmarks" ;
"~/works/"                          "unicorn_story" ;
"~/bookmarks/"                      "unicorn_story" ;
"~/works"                           "unicorn_elastic" ;
"~/bookmarks"                       "unicorn_elastic_bookmarks" ;
{noformat}
*Testing instructions*

The limits have been adjusted to allow for easier testing, so these numbers will of course not apply to real use.

* Go to one of the URLs affected by the issue
* Enter the Lockup password if necessary
* In your browser's dev tools, go to the Network tab, locate the GET request for the page, and right click on that and choose "Copy as cURL". [More info on Copy as cURL in a variety of browsers|https://ec.haxx.se/usingcurl/usingcurl-copyas].
* Paste the cURL command you just copied somewhere you can edit it, e.g. a text editor. It will look something like this:
{noformat}curl 'https://test.archiveofourown.org/collections/TheFirstCollection/bookmarks' \
-XGET \
-H 'Cookie: _otwarchive_session=keysmash; remember_user_token=keysmash; user_credentials=1; accepted_tos=20180523; lockup=secret' \
-H 'Accept: text/html,application/xhtml+xml,application/xml;q=0.9,*/*;q=0.8' \
-H 'Accept-Encoding: gzip, deflate, br' \
-H 'Host: test.archiveofourown.org' \
-H 'User-Agent: Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_15_2) AppleWebKit/605.1.15 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/13.0.4 Safari/605.1.15' \
-H 'Accept-Language: en-us' \
-H 'Referer: https://test.archiveofourown.org/collections/TheFirstCollection' \
-H 'Connection: keep-alive'{noformat}
* We want to run this command 60 times and hit a different URL each time to avoid caching. We’re going to add a line at the top telling it how many times to run ({{for i in \{1..60\}; do}}) and then modify the URL we’re hitting (here the collection name is replaced with {{$i}} – if you’re using a tag’s or user’s works or bookmarks URL, you would replace the tag or username with {{$i}}) and then end the loop at the end with {{; done}}
{noformat}for i in {1..60}; do
curl -I 'https://test.archiveofourown.org/collections/$i/bookmarks' \
-XGET \
-H 'Cookie: _otwarchive_session=keysmash; remember_user_token=keysmash; user_credentials=1; accepted_tos=20180523; lockup=secret' \
-H 'Accept: text/html,application/xhtml+xml,application/xml;q=0.9,*/*;q=0.8' \
-H 'Accept-Encoding: gzip, deflate, br' \
-H 'Host: test.archiveofourown.org' \
-H 'User-Agent: Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_15_2) AppleWebKit/605.1.15 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/13.0.4 Safari/605.1.15' \
-H 'Accept-Language: en-us' \
-H 'Referer: https://test.archiveofourown.org/collections/TheFirstCollection' \
-H 'Connection: keep-alive'; done{noformat}
* Now copy this into your command line and run it

The first output you see should list the response code as {{HTTP/2 200}}, indicating you’ve successfully reached the page, and then later ones should list {{HTTP/2 429}}, indicating you’ve been rate limited. If you try to go to any of the listed Elasticsearch page in your browser, you should get a “Retry later” message. If you try to go to a different page, e.g. the home page, you should be able to access it.

What it says on the tin\! 

We should allow {{iframe}} embeds from [archive.org|http://archive.org] that use {{src}} URLs like this:

{{<iframe src="https://archive.org/embed/jj2008-06-14.mk4&playlist=1"></iframe>}}

But not like this:

{{<iframe src="https://archive.org/dir/file.mk4&playlist=1"></iframe>}}

Or this:

{{<iframe src="https://archive.org/embed/../dir/file.mk4&playlist=1"></iframe>}}

