Admins with the superadmin or support role should be able to create, edit, and delete Known Issues.

Admins without those roles should:

* not have the “Known Issues” option under “Admin Posts” in the admin navigation menu
* not have the “Known Issues” option in admin navigation buttons on places like the new news post form ({{app/views/admin/_admin_nav.html.erb}})
* get the regular, non-admin version of the [Known Issues index|https://test.archiveofourown.org/known_issues] when following the “Known Issues” link in the footer or otherwise attempting to access the URL for the Known Issues index ({{https://test.archiveofourown.org/known_issues}})
* be redirected and given an error message if they enter the following URLs
** {{https://test.archiveofourown.org/known_issues/new}}
** {{https://test.archiveofourown.org/known_issues/1/edit}}
** {{https://test.archiveofourown.org/known_issues/1}}

Admins with the superadmin, docs, support, and translation roles should be able to post, modify, and delete FAQs. (Bonus points if admins with the translation role can only modify FAQs that are translations! But we can push this to a separate issue for later.)

Admins without those roles should:

* not have the “Archive FAQ” option under “Admin Posts” in the admin navigation menu
* not have the “Archive FAQ” in the admin navigation buttons ({{app/views/admin/_admin_nav.html.erb}}), shown on pages like the wrangling guidelines page when logged in as a tag wrangling admin 
* get the regular, non-admin version of the [FAQ index|https://test.archiveofourown.org/faq] when following the “FAQ” link in the main navigation or otherwise attempting to access the URL for the FAQ index ({{https://test.archiveofourown.org/faq}})
* not have the “Updated: [Date]” info or “Edit” link in an h2 on the top of the page when accessing a specific category (e.g., {{https://test.archiveofourown.org/faq/category_name?language_id=en}})
** i.e., it should look the same as it does when _not_ logged in as admin
* be redirected and given an error message if they enter the following URLs 
** {{https://test.archiveofourown.org/faq/new?language_id=en}}
** {{https://test.archiveofourown.org/faq/manage?language_id=en}}
** {{https://test.archiveofourown.org/faq/category_name/edit?language_id=en}}
** {{https://test.archiveofourown.org/faq/category_name/questions/manage}}
** {{https://test.archiveofourown.org/faq/category_name/confirm_delete?language_id=en}}

*Testing note*: In the above URLs, {{category_name}} is a placeholder needs to be replaced with an FAQ category that is available on staging such as {{posting-and-editing}} or {{collections-and-challenges}}.

The topmost yellow caution message on the [+New Orphan+|https://archiveofourown.org/orphans/new] form page currently says:

{quote}Orphaning will *permanently* remove all identifying data from the following work(s), their chapters, associated series, and any feedback replies you may have left on them.{quote}

However, this isn’t correct. Only the bylines of these objects will be affected – if the user posted their identifying information anywhere else, it won’t be automatically removed by the orphaning process. 

This caution message should be updated to read:

{quote}Orphaning will *permanently* remove your username and/or pseud from the bylines of: the following work(s), their chapters, associated series, and any comments you may have left on them while logged into this account.{quote}

Another yellow caution message should be added immediately beneath this one, saying: 

{quote}Orphaning will automatically remove your personal information from *bylines only*. It will *not* automatically remove your personal information from anywhere else in the work(s). Social media accounts, contact information, email addresses, names, and any other personal information posted in the title, summary, notes, tags, work body, or comment text will *not* be automatically removed. Comments posted by other users will also *not* be affected by Orphaning. If you want information removed from these places, you should edit or delete it prior to Orphaning. *Once you Orphan the work(s), you will no longer be able to delete information in these places yourself.*{quote}

h1. Steps to reproduce

# Log in
# Choose an adventure:
## Hi, username! > My Dashboard > Skins > Create Site Skin
## Hi, username! > My Dashboard > Skins > My Work Skins > Create Work Skin
# Enter CSS like {{.a { color-scheme: dark }}}
# Submit

h1. What happens

An error saying {{color-scheme}} is not allowed.

h1. What should happen

It should be possible to make a site or work skin using the [color-scheme CSS property|https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/color-scheme] to control whether certain elements (e.g., scroll bars and form elements) should be shown in the system’s dark or light mode. 

All of the following values should be allowed:

{noformat}color-scheme: normal;
color-scheme: light;
color-scheme: dark;
color-scheme: light dark;
color-scheme: dark light;
color-scheme: only light;
color-scheme: only dark;
color-scheme: inherit;
color-scheme: initial;
color-scheme: revert;
color-scheme: revert-layer;
color-scheme: unset;{noformat}

h1. Testing

Put the following into a skin and make sure that after saving, the output matches the input and you don't get any error messages. Note that this won’t actually lead to any visual changes; we’re just trying to make sure all the values are accepted by our system. 

{noformat}.a { color-scheme: normal; }
.b { color-scheme: light; }
.c { color-scheme: dark; }
.d { color-scheme: light dark; }
.e { color-scheme: dark light; }
.f { color-scheme: only light; }
.g { color-scheme: only dark; }
.h { color-scheme: inherit; }
.i { color-scheme: initial; }
.j { color-scheme: revert; }
.k { color-scheme: revert-layer; }
.l { color-scheme: unset; }{noformat}

You’ll also need to check the skins help file – the ? by the CSS field – and make sure the new properties are all listed.

*Deploy Notes*

This requires running the recache skins playbook (it does all static assets not just skins).

To help the Support committee with their ticket volume, we should add the following text to CONTRIBUTING.md anywhere we mention “please [contact the AO3 Support team|https://archiveofourown.org/support]”.

{quote}Our Support team is staffed by volunteers, so please wait for a response before submitting another ticket. Duplicate submissions will not make things happen faster.{quote}

Additionally, we can highlight ADT’s own email list by adding

{quote}We do not have a public chat, but you are welcome to contact us at [otw-coders@transformativeworks.org|mailto:otw-coders@transformativeworks.org] if you have any questions.{quote}

to the README’s ["How to contribute" section|https://github.com/otwcode/otwarchive/tree/d1a63622444b1d7b0ba1f4b9b3c77896178a5c20?tab=readme-ov-file#how-to-contribute].

We’d like to allow use of [aspect-ratio|https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/aspect-ratio] in skins. 

For values, it should accept:

#  the {{auto}} keyword
# whole numbers ({{1}})
# decimal numbers ({{0.5}})
# [ratios|https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/ratio] ({{16/9}}), which should be allowed to have 
## spaces before the slash
## spaces after the slash
## spaces both before and after the slash
## spaces on neither side of the slash
## decimals
# the {{auto}} keyword *before* a 
## whole number,
## decimal number, or
## ratio
# the auto keyword *after* a
## whole number, 
## decimal number, or
## ratio

The help popup at [https://test.archiveofourown.org/help/skins-creating.html|https://test.archiveofourown.org/help/skins-creating.html] will also need to be updated:

# {{aspect-ratio}} will need to be listed under “We also allow the following specific properties”
# the “Numeric Values” section will need to be updated according to the fix:
## assuming the fix only allows ratios for {{aspect-ratio}}, this sentence should be added above the “PS”: “For the aspect-ratio property, you can specify ratios using numeric values up to three decimal places."
## if ratios have to be allowed everywhere numbers are accepted, the text should instead be amended to say: “You can specify numeric values up to three decimal places, either as percentages or ratios or in [various units|https://w3schools.com/css/css_units.asp]:” (the “or ratios” is new)

h1. Testing

To test, you can just make sure our CSS sanitizer accepts the property and the desired formats for the values. Whether or not they work is the browser’s problem, not ours. 😆 

# Log in
# Hi, username! > My Dashboard > Skins > Create Site Skin
# Fill in the Title field
# Next to the “CSS” heading/label, use the “?” help symbol to open the help pop-up and ensure it includes the text provided above.
# Close the help pop-up
# Enter the CSS provided below these instructions in the CSS field
# Press Submit

All but the last four rules ({{.invalid1}}, {{.invalid2}}, {{.invalid3}}, and {{.invalid4}}) in this CSS should be permitted.

{code:css}.class1 { aspect-ratio: banana }
.class2 { aspect-ratio: 1 }
.class3 { aspect-ratio: 0.5 }
.class4a { aspect-ratio: 16 /9 }
.class4b { aspect-ratio: 16/ 9 }
.class4c { aspect-ratio: 16 / 9}
.class4d { aspect-ratio: 16/9 }
.class4e { aspect-ratio: 1/1.75 }
.class5a { aspect-ratio: auto 1 }
.class5b { aspect-ratio: auto 0.25 }
.class5c { aspect-ratio: auto 4/3 }
.class6a { aspect-ratio: 1 auto }
.class6b { aspect-ratio: 0.25 auto }
.class6c { aspect-ratio: 0.5/ 1 auto }
.invalid1 { aspect-ratio: 1,300 }
.invalid2 { aspect-ratio: 100% }
.invalid3 { aspect-ratio: auto
auto ; }
.invalid4 {
  aspect-ratio: 1
auto
url(http://foo.com/bar.png);
}{code}

The help text at [https://test.archiveofourown.org/help/skins-creating.html|https://test.archiveofourown.org/help/skins-creating.html] says:

{quote}We allow external image URLs (specified as url('http://somesite.com/my_awesome_image.jpg') in JPG, GIF, and PNG formats.{quote}

Let’s change that to [https://example.com/my_awesome_image.jpg|https://example.com/my_awesome_image.jpg] instead, since [example.com|http://example.com] exists for this purpose and can never be bought for nefarious purposes.

Per several user requests and ADT approval, embeds from [audio.com|http://audio.com] should be allowed. Hosting site is stable and from reputed sources. Sample embed code is 

{{<div style="height: 228px; width: 600px;"><iframe src="https://audio.com/embed/audio/1795710633346764?theme=image "}}
{{    style="display:block; border-radius: 1px; border: none; height: 204px; width: 600px;"></iframe><a href='https://audio.com/qwuin ' style="text-align: center; display: block; color: #A4ABB6; font-size: 12px; font-family: sans-serif; line-height: 16px; margin-top: 8px; overflow: hidden; white-space: nowrap; text-overflow: ellipsis;">@qwuin</a></div>}}

sanitizer list is at [https://github.com/otwcode/otwarchive/blob/master/lib/otw_sanitize/embed_sanitizer.rb|https://github.com/otwcode/otwarchive/blob/master/lib/otw_sanitize/embed_sanitizer.rb]

h2. Testing

Try to create a work with an embed from audio.com.

Trying to create a bookmark on production fails with this error:

{quote}{{Mysql2::Error: Out of range value for column 'id' at row 1 (Mysql2::Error)}}{quote}

The last bookmark created on production has the ID 2147483647, which is the last ID you can use with an INT column.

