Description:
h1. Steps to reproduce

# Log in
# Choose an adventure:
## Hi, username! > My Dashboard > Skins > Create Site Skin
## Hi, username! > My Dashboard > Skins > My Work Skins > Create Work Skin
# Enter CSS like {{.a { fill: #900 } .aa { stroke: darkred; } .aaa { stroke-width: 2px; }}}
# Submit

h1. What happens

An error saying the properties are not allowed.

h1. What should happen

It should be possible to make a site or work skin using the [fill CSS property|https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/fill] to adjust the fill color of SVG images, [stroke|https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/stroke] to adjust the stroke color, and [stroke-width|https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/stroke-width] to adjust the stroke size.

All of the following values should be allowed:

{noformat}fill: darkred;
fill: #900;
fill: rgba(0, 200, 0, 0.5);
fill: hsl(228 4% 24%);
fill: none;
stroke: darkred;
stroke: #900;
stroke: rgba(0 200 0);
stroke: hsl(228 4% 24%);
stroke: none;
stroke-width: 100%;
stroke-width: 1cm;
stroke-width: 1em;
stroke-width: 1ex;
stroke-width: 1in;
stroke-width: 1mm;
stroke-width: 1pc;
stroke-width: 1pt;
stroke-width: 1px;{noformat}

h1. Testing

Put the following into a skin and make sure that after saving, the output matches the input and you don't get any error messages. Note that this won’t actually lead to any visual changes; we’re just trying to make sure all the values are accepted by our system. 

{noformat}.a { fill: darkred; }
.b { fill: #900; }
.c { fill: rgb(0 200 0); }
.d { fill: hsl(228 4% 24%); }
.aa { stroke: darkred; }
.bb { stroke: #900; }
.cc { stroke: rgb(0, 200, 0); }
.dd { stroke: hsl(228 4% 24%); }
.ee { stroke: none; }
.aaa { stroke-width: 100%; }
.bbb { stroke-width: 1cm; }
.ccc { stroke-width: 1em; }
.ddd { stroke-width: 1ex; }
.eee { stroke-width: 1in; } 
.fff { stroke-width: 1mm; }
.hhh { stroke-width: 1pc; }
.iii { stroke-width: 1pt; }
.jjj { stroke-width: 1px; }{noformat}

Additionally, please make sure the following produces error messages about the values not being allowed (there will also be a message saying “There don't seem to be any rules for [selector]”):

{noformat}.a { fill: url("https://ao3.org/image.png"); }
.b { fill: url("https://ao3.org/image.png") darkred; }
.c { fill: url("/image.png"); }
.d { fill: url("/image.png") darkred; }
.aa { stroke: url("https://ao3.org/image.png"); }{noformat}

(The above isn’t strictly necessary to include given how we limit URLs, but color adjustments are the main thing we want to allow, and forbidding {{url()}} is default behavior for us.)

You’ll also need to check the skins help file – the ? by the CSS field – and make sure the new properties are listed.

There are several similar gift exchange-related notifications currently in {{UserMailer}}. They should be moved to {{GiftExchangeMailer}}, which was added in [https://otwarchive.atlassian.net/browse/AO3-6277|https://otwarchive.atlassian.net/browse/AO3-6277|smart-link]. These notifications are:

* {{assignments_sent_notification}}
* {{assignment_default_notification}}
* {{invalid_signup_notification}}
* {{potential_match_generation_notification}}

h2. Testing

On the gift exchange mailer preview page ([https://test.archiveofourown.org/rails/mailers/gift_exchange_mailer|https://test.archiveofourown.org/rails/mailers/gift_exchange_mailer]), each of the notifications should have a “collection email” and a “maintainer” preview listed. Each of the previews should be an email without errors or exposed HTML in the HTML and plain-text versions.

h2. Notes

In [these commits|https://github.com/otwcode/otwarchive/pull/5512/changes/cc5e76c69ac46d50012550011d6adf6064050671..5926ab5a507dbb11d0d2d777a9dd34bcd18ebecc] the {{GiftExchangeMailer}} was added and a new notification was moved into it - they can be used as a reference for the kind of changes that need to be made.

The Content Policy notice at the bottom of the posting form should be updated to remove the words “you post”:

{noformat}<p class="notice">All works on AO3 must comply with our <a href="/content">Content Policy</a>. For more information, please refer to our <a href="/tos_faq#content_faq">Terms of Service FAQ</a>.</p> {noformat}

This notice appears in [3 places in the current code|https://github.com/otwcode/otwarchive/blob/master/config/locales/views/en.yml]; and should display when posting, editing, or previewing a work, chapter, draft, work tags, or when importing a work.

